WEBVTT

00:03.134 --> 00:06.971
Arrow, where are you taking me?

00:08.056 --> 00:10.391
You want to skewer
this man's soul, too?

00:10.600 --> 00:15.100
That boy will make
my sixth Stand user…

00:15.605 --> 00:18.107
That should be more than enough.

00:18.233 --> 00:22.733
I'll eliminate any wretch who dares
get close to my dear, Yoshikage!

00:27.951 --> 00:29.827
TING

00:30.370 --> 00:31.204
What?!

00:36.542 --> 00:37.251
Ow.

00:37.252 --> 00:39.379
W-What the blazes?

00:39.629 --> 00:43.466
The arrow chose him,
but was deflected.

00:47.929 --> 00:49.639
<i>Breakdown, Breakdown</i>

00:50.306 --> 00:52.433
<i>(Listen up)
Breakdown, Breakdown</i>

00:53.184 --> 00:55.144
<i>(Listen)
Breakdown, Breakdown</i>

00:56.396 --> 00:59.482
<i>Breakdown, Breakdown
(3, 2, 1) Let's Go!</i>

00:59.524 --> 01:00.650
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE
DIAMOND IS UNBREAKABLE

01:00.733 --> 01:05.233
<i>Shining Justice begins to sprout</i>

01:06.281 --> 01:10.781
<i>Brand-new bed town
Will we meet? Let's find out</i>

01:11.953 --> 01:16.453
<i>Feeling the sea breeze from the cape
through the tunnel to the tower</i>

01:17.542 --> 01:22.042
<i>We wander into the alley,
drawn to each other</i>

01:22.839 --> 01:27.339
<i>A shadow melts into our hearts</i>

01:30.221 --> 01:34.721
<i>But the golden spirits
shine a light to protect us</i>

01:40.106 --> 01:44.606
<i>Let the voice of love
take you higher</i>

01:45.111 --> 01:49.611
<i>Let the gathering forces
overcome time itself</i>

01:51.451 --> 01:55.951
<i>1999 Bizarre Summer</i>

01:56.372 --> 02:00.872
<i>Our courage keeps the town in bloom</i>

02:01.961 --> 02:06.131
<i>Great Days</i>

02:09.010 --> 02:13.055
EPISODE 27
I'M AN ALIEN

02:10.178 --> 02:13.077
Every piece of intel we could find
lies in that envelope.

02:13.514 --> 02:14.890
PROFILE
YOSHIKAGE KIRA

02:14.265 --> 02:14.912
He's done a fine job
of covering his tracks.

02:19.187 --> 02:20.646
Yoshikage Kira…

02:20.938 --> 02:23.815
Who's face are you hiding behind,
who's name have you stolen?

02:24.359 --> 02:25.818
Where are you?

02:26.319 --> 02:27.653
Summer…

02:27.695 --> 02:31.198
Tourist season here in Morioh.

02:32.325 --> 02:33.326
Yeah…

02:34.118 --> 02:37.329
I doubt he'll be able to
stay quiet for long.

02:38.331 --> 02:39.665
There's no way he can
resist his urges.

02:39.707 --> 02:41.458
He'll be itching to act.

02:41.542 --> 02:43.919
<i>It's finally summer, everyone.</i>

02:44.212 --> 02:46.339
<i>If you hadn't noticed,
July 1st marked the opening of</i>

02:46.381 --> 02:48.591
<i>Morioh's beautiful rivers and be aches.</i>

02:48.841 --> 02:52.177
<i>With masses of tourists descending
on our town from S City and beyond,</i>

02:52.220 --> 02:54.096
<i>little ol' Morioh
is bound to be hopping.</i>

02:54.472 --> 02:58.267
<i>Whether it's a little r and r,
camping, fishing, or yachting…</i>

02:58.434 --> 03:02.604
<i>Morioh is your special summer paradise!</i>

03:02.647 --> 03:06.233
<i>Now how are you going to
make the most of your summer?</i>

03:06.442 --> 03:09.194
<i>A summer paradise, indeed…</i>

03:09.654 --> 03:12.156
<i>Not just for them, but for him, too…</i>

03:12.281 --> 03:14.491
<i>A summer paradise, indeed</i>

03:16.327 --> 03:20.827
<i>We live our lives concealing
our deepest hopes and fears.</i>

03:21.499 --> 03:22.541
<i>But…</i>

03:22.583 --> 03:24.167
<i>To conceal forever, to everyone…</i>

03:24.335 --> 03:28.255
<i>Can one live a lifetime
behind a veil of secrecy?</i>

03:31.426 --> 03:32.301
<i>Damn it!</i>

03:32.552 --> 03:36.514
<i>I want her to see
the true Yoshikage Kira.</i>

03:36.973 --> 03:39.725
<i>To hear from my lips
the passion that burns within me…</i>

03:39.767 --> 03:42.144
<i>To feel my hands wrapped
around her delicate neck,</i>

03:42.186 --> 03:44.605
<i>as I wring the life from her heart.</i>

03:46.232 --> 03:49.818
<i>As my nail growth surges,
so do my carnal desires.</i>

03:51.112 --> 03:54.490
<i>I just need to persevere
until the urge subsides.</i>

03:56.033 --> 04:00.162
<i>I still haven't mastered his signature.</i>

03:58.953 --> 04:01.413
KOSAKU KAWAJIRI

04:01.456 --> 04:05.956
KOSAKU

04:08.963 --> 04:13.258
<i>Josuke Higashikata… Jotaro Kujo…</i>

04:13.301 --> 04:15.803
<i>They're the reason
I'm in this predicament.</i>

04:20.766 --> 04:22.058
Um…

04:22.143 --> 04:25.312
Uh… May I… ask what
you might be up to?

04:29.066 --> 04:32.444
You're right.
I should just open my eyes.

04:32.945 --> 04:34.988
You're reading a book.

04:35.031 --> 04:37.199
Um, I made you some tea.

04:37.283 --> 04:40.619
I know I don't usually
do this sort of thing,

04:40.912 --> 04:43.039
b-but I thought maybe…

04:43.498 --> 04:45.958
If you don't want any,
that's fine, too…

05:04.060 --> 05:06.771
Oh, it's so late.

05:06.854 --> 05:09.231
I suppose I should hit the sack…

05:30.503 --> 05:33.088
<i>Bare your heart to her.</i>

05:33.422 --> 05:35.841
<i>Reveal to her your true self,</i>

05:36.259 --> 05:37.969
<i>Yoshikage Kira.</i>

05:45.726 --> 05:47.310
Honey?

05:47.395 --> 05:50.523
<i>Shit. Baring my soul was a mistake.</i>

05:50.565 --> 05:52.358
<i>They'll figure me out.</i>

05:55.570 --> 05:58.447
Sorry to have frightened you.

05:59.740 --> 06:03.160
<i>H-He was trying to unbutton my blouse?</i>

06:03.786 --> 06:06.288
<i>"Sorry to have frightened you"?</i>

06:06.372 --> 06:09.708
<i>Don't be sorry! This new you is…</i>

06:10.084 --> 06:12.127
<i>is terribly exciting!</i>

06:12.211 --> 06:16.465
<i>It's actually kind of turning me on! I…</i>

06:16.674 --> 06:18.509
<i>I've fallen</i>

06:18.593 --> 06:20.469
<i>in love with you.</i>

06:27.685 --> 06:31.355
J-Josuke, I-look over there.

06:31.439 --> 06:32.898
What the heck is—

06:39.113 --> 06:42.157
Is this… Could this be…

06:42.241 --> 06:43.450
T-Terri Funk—

06:43.492 --> 06:44.784
It's a crop circle!

06:44.827 --> 06:46.954
Yeah! A crop circle!

06:46.996 --> 06:48.747
Th-That's amazing!

06:48.789 --> 06:52.125
To think one would pop up
in some field in Morioh!

06:52.168 --> 06:55.004
Something's not right, Okuyasu.

06:55.421 --> 06:58.173
Look closely, at the middle.

07:03.888 --> 07:05.639
Shit, I can't believe this!

07:07.183 --> 07:08.726
You're going in?

07:08.809 --> 07:10.811
We don't have a choice!

07:14.649 --> 07:16.317
Be careful.

07:16.359 --> 07:17.651
Yeah.

07:20.488 --> 07:22.490
I-Is he alive?

07:22.531 --> 07:25.534
Well, he's got a little
scratch on the back of his neck,

07:25.618 --> 07:27.536
but I think he only fainted.

07:27.828 --> 07:30.413
Hey, wake up.
Are you all right? Hey!

07:30.498 --> 07:34.210
I've never seen him
around at our school.

07:35.252 --> 07:37.754
Oh, I think he's come to.

07:50.601 --> 07:52.019
Where…

07:52.770 --> 07:54.772
Where am I?

07:54.855 --> 07:56.064
Where?

07:56.107 --> 07:59.610
You're in the middle of
a field in Budogaoka, Morioh.

07:59.860 --> 08:01.820
Is this Earth?

08:02.780 --> 08:07.075
Yesterday evening,
I remember I suddenly felt unwell.

08:07.159 --> 08:09.995
I must have then fell unconscious.

08:10.413 --> 08:11.956
It is now past eight o'clock,

08:12.039 --> 08:16.539
so I estimate I was unconscious
for nearly thirteen Earth hours.

08:21.882 --> 08:24.759
You really had us going there!

08:25.219 --> 08:28.931
Damn! That was one damn good prank!

08:28.973 --> 08:31.392
Man, you got me good!

08:31.434 --> 08:33.811
Dude, you are hilarious!

08:34.103 --> 08:37.397
You made your own crop circle
and then waited

08:37.440 --> 08:39.775
in a bunch of weeds
for someone to come by?

08:39.817 --> 08:41.568
Amazing! Simply amazing!

08:41.610 --> 08:44.154
I can't breathe! My stomach hurts!

08:44.363 --> 08:45.489
STOMACH MEDICINE

08:50.661 --> 08:51.953
It's freakin' ridiculous!

08:53.289 --> 08:55.457
Which school do you go to?

08:55.875 --> 08:58.586
- You're just our kind of guy!
- School?

08:58.627 --> 09:01.379
My home planet once lay in
one of the Magellanic Clouds,

09:01.422 --> 09:03.590
but has since been destroyed.

09:04.091 --> 09:07.052
I've journeyed to earth to survey

09:07.094 --> 09:10.472
the livability of its land
and the amiability of its people.

09:12.391 --> 09:15.644
Quit while you're ahead.
That was an epic prank,

09:15.686 --> 09:18.313
don't spoil it by trying too hard.

09:18.397 --> 09:19.815
Here, have a tissue.

09:27.615 --> 09:30.492
Thank you.
That was quite palatable.

09:31.952 --> 09:34.663
Well, we really should be
getting to school.

09:34.705 --> 09:36.665
Y-Yeah, you're right.

09:36.749 --> 09:38.167
Let's go.

09:39.960 --> 09:42.379
He decimated that tissue.

09:42.463 --> 09:44.673
Someone thinks they're a comedian.

09:46.050 --> 09:48.677
The ice cream store's closed!

09:48.719 --> 09:52.139
It's the only thing that
makes Monday mornings bearable…

09:52.181 --> 09:53.432
Nothing we can do about it.

09:53.474 --> 09:55.267
Just forget about it.

09:55.392 --> 09:57.685
Care for some ice cream?

09:58.312 --> 10:00.522
Well? Would you like some?

10:00.648 --> 10:04.068
Yeah, but the place's closed,
we're shit out of luck now.

10:04.151 --> 10:05.986
That's no reason to give up.

10:06.153 --> 10:08.363
I just so happen to have two here.

10:08.781 --> 10:12.159
Consider it a quid pro quo
for the tissues.

10:13.452 --> 10:16.455
Earth seems quite livable indeed.

10:17.248 --> 10:18.374
It's cold…

10:18.415 --> 10:21.876
W-Why do you have
ice cream cones in your bag?

10:22.002 --> 10:24.212
Is the ice cream unsatisfactory?

10:24.296 --> 10:27.966
That's not the point!
Who the hell are you?

10:28.342 --> 10:31.636
I believe I already told you…

10:31.679 --> 10:34.932
Ah! You want me
to introduce myself.

10:35.015 --> 10:36.349
How could I forget…

10:36.642 --> 10:40.479
My name is Nu Mikitakazo Nushi.

10:40.521 --> 10:42.689
I am 216 years old.

10:43.023 --> 10:45.275
I am a spaceship pilot.

10:45.359 --> 10:47.277
I like having pets.

10:48.153 --> 10:51.573
I'm currently carrying
a house mouse in my bag.

10:51.615 --> 10:53.992
He adores it when I brush his back.

10:54.243 --> 10:56.995
<i>This freak's a Stand user.
No doubt about it.</i>

10:57.037 --> 10:58.747
<i>Let's show him
what a hospital looks like!</i>

10:58.831 --> 11:00.541
<i>Hold your horses, Okuyasu.</i>

11:00.583 --> 11:02.334
<i>Do you really think a Stand user</i>

11:02.376 --> 11:05.420
<i>would say that he's from
the Magellanic Clouds?</i>

11:05.462 --> 11:08.548
<i>- Then what the hell is he?</i>
- There, there, there.

11:08.591 --> 11:10.259
<i>I don't have the foggiest idea.</i>

11:10.342 --> 11:12.010
<i>Time to conduct our own survey.</i>

11:12.052 --> 11:14.012
<i>Don't eat that ice cream.</i>

11:14.179 --> 11:15.138
<i>Huh?!</i>

11:16.557 --> 11:19.101
So you're 216, huh?

11:19.226 --> 11:19.976
Yes.

11:20.019 --> 11:22.312
- Hmm…
- Hmm…

11:24.356 --> 11:27.359
So you're a spaceship pilot?

11:28.319 --> 11:30.779
Why do you keep mimicking me?

11:31.238 --> 11:32.781
So, what?

11:32.865 --> 11:37.365
You trying to say you're an alien?

11:40.456 --> 11:41.623
An alien!

11:41.749 --> 11:43.167
An alien! Yes!

11:43.417 --> 11:45.419
I suppose I should have
mentioned that initially.

11:45.586 --> 11:47.087
I am an alien.

11:47.129 --> 11:48.463
Hey, hey, hey, hey…

11:48.547 --> 11:51.383
So, then, you have a…
flying saucer?

11:51.467 --> 11:53.844
Could you call over your spaceship?

11:54.053 --> 11:55.387
You can, right?

11:55.429 --> 11:56.430
Of course.

11:56.472 --> 11:58.223
Unfortunately,
it is currently standing by

11:58.265 --> 12:00.642
at an altitude of
1,500,000 kilometers,

12:00.684 --> 12:02.310
so it would take
approximately three days.

12:02.353 --> 12:03.771
Anything else is futile.

12:03.812 --> 12:05.980
Do you call it with that watch?

12:06.023 --> 12:08.275
Oh, how did you know?

12:08.567 --> 12:11.069
But this must stay
between the three of us.

12:11.111 --> 12:13.321
You must not share this
with anyone.

12:13.656 --> 12:16.283
<i>This guy's more than a little cuckoo.</i>

12:16.325 --> 12:18.618
<i>That wasn't some innocent little prank.</i>

12:18.661 --> 12:20.454
<i>He's a delusional psychopath.</i>

12:20.496 --> 12:21.955
<i>Maybe I should knock
that nose ring to the floor?</i>

12:21.997 --> 12:24.499
<i>You always let your fists
do the talking.</i>

12:24.541 --> 12:26.834
<i>Just to be sure,
let's dig a little deeper.</i>

12:27.127 --> 12:29.671
Do you have some kinda ray gun or

12:29.755 --> 12:32.340
or ultra hyper anti-gravity device
in there?

12:32.716 --> 12:34.342
Of course I do.

12:34.510 --> 12:37.346
But I did not journey here
to engage in conflict,

12:37.388 --> 12:39.181
so I left them in my spaceship.

12:39.223 --> 12:41.266
Aw, come on.

12:41.308 --> 12:44.060
You're an alien,
show us something cool.

12:44.144 --> 12:47.522
And your blood wasn't even green.

12:47.564 --> 12:50.858
Yeah. Alien blood is always green.

12:51.610 --> 12:54.154
Do you doubt
my extraterrestrialness?

12:54.196 --> 12:55.405
Hey, calm down.

12:55.489 --> 12:57.782
You finally figured it out,
huh, dumb-ass!

12:57.992 --> 12:59.868
I can deal with a little prank
here and there,

12:59.952 --> 13:02.704
but I refuse to shoot the breeze
with a lunatic like you.

13:02.788 --> 13:04.498
I cannot believe
you just said that!

13:04.540 --> 13:07.543
Shut up! It's always better
to say it like it is!

13:10.004 --> 13:12.548
What? Did a fire
break out somewhere?

13:23.600 --> 13:25.351
W-What the hell?

13:25.686 --> 13:28.105
This sound…
I can't stand this sound.

13:28.188 --> 13:29.981
This sound…

13:30.065 --> 13:32.484
Stop this sound!

13:32.693 --> 13:34.403
I can't stand this sound!

13:34.611 --> 13:36.529
I'm allergic to this sound!

13:36.572 --> 13:37.990
Make it stop!

13:40.659 --> 13:42.661
Josuke, this guy's dangerous!

13:42.703 --> 13:45.247
Let's go. We should
stay far away from him.

13:45.330 --> 13:47.081
Yeah, but…

13:47.124 --> 13:49.501
We can't just
abandon him like that.

13:49.543 --> 13:52.420
He said it was just allergies.
Leave him be.

13:52.546 --> 13:54.214
I'm outta here, Josuke.

13:54.256 --> 13:55.757
H-Hey!

13:55.966 --> 13:58.426
Damn it, Okuyasu.

14:02.014 --> 14:04.933
H-Hey, you okay?

14:04.975 --> 14:07.769
Please, take me away…

14:07.811 --> 14:10.230
take me away from this sound…

14:12.649 --> 14:14.275
W-What?!

14:14.318 --> 14:16.069
Take me away from this sound!

14:16.111 --> 14:18.279
So then you're a…

14:18.530 --> 14:22.617
I have the power to
transform into anything.

14:22.701 --> 14:26.871
H-Hurry… This sound
is going to split my head in two…

14:26.914 --> 14:27.998
I beg you…

14:28.415 --> 14:32.460
I'll turn into sneakers, so please,
put them on and get me out of here!

14:33.712 --> 14:36.589
In return,
I'll do anything you ask!

14:38.133 --> 14:40.301
Are you a Stand user?!

14:44.556 --> 14:46.683
Whoa! Y-Your speed is amazing!

14:46.767 --> 14:48.935
With your power and
my power combined,

14:48.977 --> 14:52.647
our speed and jumping ability
are doubled.

14:52.731 --> 14:55.775
Are you really an alien?!

14:59.238 --> 15:01.990
TERRA VENTUS

15:04.660 --> 15:06.578
What the hell is going on?!

15:14.211 --> 15:14.961
You…

15:16.046 --> 15:17.630
You can't see this?

15:20.634 --> 15:21.843
<i>He can't see it!</i>

15:22.010 --> 15:23.678
<i>He's not a Stand user.</i>

15:23.971 --> 15:26.348
<i>Then what the hell is this power?</i>

15:26.515 --> 15:28.141
What the hell are you?!

15:28.308 --> 15:29.851
You are stubborn, aren't you?

15:29.977 --> 15:31.853
I have been telling you
I am an alien…

15:31.895 --> 15:33.813
Just give me a second.

15:34.022 --> 15:36.983
I've gotta wrap my head
around this.

15:37.609 --> 15:40.653
Anyhow, I appreciate
your saving me from that situation.

15:40.821 --> 15:44.825
The people on my planet
truly abhor the sound of sirens.

15:45.117 --> 15:47.202
It is a very upsetting
wavelength for us.

15:47.536 --> 15:51.414
I would like to repay your kindness
for rescuing me.

15:52.499 --> 15:54.209
Shall I turn into a fan
to refresh you?

15:54.501 --> 15:57.587
Or perhaps a back scratcher
to scratch your back?

15:57.671 --> 16:01.383
Whoa, I didn't save you cause
I wanted a favor from you…

16:04.511 --> 16:07.889
You'll really do anything?
Okay! Then do it! Pretty please!

16:04.595 --> 16:09.095
SHOPPING
CATALOG

16:08.056 --> 16:09.954
What is it that you request of me?

16:10.267 --> 16:12.686
C-Can you turn into anything?

16:12.811 --> 16:15.188
Like something light,
or multiples of something?

16:15.230 --> 16:17.899
Yes. I can transform
into nearly anything.

16:18.108 --> 16:20.235
However,
becoming complex machinery

16:20.277 --> 16:22.237
or anything more powerful than me
is unfeasible.

16:22.571 --> 16:26.324
I see, I see. Got it. I like you!

16:26.783 --> 16:28.534
So you want to thank me, right?

16:28.577 --> 16:29.244
Yes.

16:29.244 --> 16:30.912
You know I just…

16:31.038 --> 16:33.123
thought of a great idea.

16:33.457 --> 16:36.084
It's gonna be a win-win
for all parties involved.

16:36.293 --> 16:37.085
Win-win?

16:37.169 --> 16:37.919
Yeah!

16:38.712 --> 16:42.841
See, I won a little spending money
recently in the local lottery,

16:43.008 --> 16:46.678
then my mom found out
and froze my account.

16:47.054 --> 16:50.265
Once that woman makes up her mind,
your fate is sealed.

16:50.557 --> 16:54.060
Being flat broke for the summer
is the worst.

16:56.188 --> 16:57.647
SHOPPING
CATALOG

16:56.772 --> 16:57.669
That's why…

16:58.440 --> 17:00.442
Can you turn into this? Right here.

17:03.737 --> 17:05.405
What is that?

17:05.530 --> 17:07.365
They're called dice!

17:07.449 --> 17:09.117
I'll make some cash with these,

17:09.159 --> 17:12.370
then split the winnings with you,
thus creating a win-win situation!

17:12.579 --> 17:14.706
What do they do?

17:14.915 --> 17:17.334
Huh? You don't know what dice are?

17:17.668 --> 17:19.461
My apologies…

17:19.628 --> 17:21.796
It's nothing to be sorry for.

17:21.838 --> 17:24.632
It's super easy. I'll show you.

17:24.925 --> 17:28.762
Anyone who likes playing games
goes nuts over these things.

17:28.887 --> 17:31.431
They've got six sides
and are made from hard material.

17:31.640 --> 17:34.643
This dot represents the number one,

17:34.685 --> 17:36.269
and each face has
a different number, up to six.

17:36.353 --> 17:38.521
Ah, yes.
It's starting to make sense.

17:38.689 --> 17:41.108
So five dots means
the number five, right?

17:41.233 --> 17:42.609
Impressive, Mr. alien!

17:42.651 --> 17:45.654
- And three dots represent a three.
- Yes! Try turning into one.

17:45.946 --> 17:47.614
At your service, Sir.

17:48.448 --> 17:49.574
It is simple.

17:50.409 --> 17:53.954
I think you're a little confused.
You went a little too big.

17:54.246 --> 17:55.830
I'm thinkin' this big.

17:55.872 --> 17:57.665
Also, you've got five on two sides.

17:57.749 --> 18:00.042
Each face has a different
number of dots from one to six.

18:00.168 --> 18:03.212
The numbers on one side and its
opposite side should equal seven.

18:03.297 --> 18:04.798
Oh, my apologies.

18:07.092 --> 18:08.635
How's this?

18:12.306 --> 18:13.515
Th-That tickles!

18:13.598 --> 18:16.809
Hey, don't laugh.
Dice aren't supposed to talk.

18:16.977 --> 18:17.852
Huh?

18:18.061 --> 18:19.187
Come on.

18:19.229 --> 18:20.730
I-I'll try harder.

18:20.856 --> 18:23.400
I'm a bit nervous about this, but…

18:24.568 --> 18:28.363
Yes, you're good! Very good!
This is perfect!

18:28.405 --> 18:30.281
Now I'm getting excited!

18:30.324 --> 18:31.408
Rohan Kishibe,

18:31.491 --> 18:34.285
- you better have some cashola ready!
- I-I can't breathe…

18:36.038 --> 18:38.373
Oh, well what a surprise.

18:38.498 --> 18:41.501
Now why would Josuke Higashikata
be visiting me?

18:42.002 --> 18:44.212
This is certainly
out of the ordinary.

18:44.588 --> 18:46.881
Did you uncover more dirt on Kira?

18:47.382 --> 18:50.176
No, not exactly…

18:50.218 --> 18:51.886
Um, well…

18:52.012 --> 18:54.556
So, finished with work for the day?

18:54.681 --> 18:58.184
I was wondering if you'd let me
take a peek at the next volume…

18:59.519 --> 19:01.354
Just what are you scheming now?

19:01.480 --> 19:02.689
Come on, spit it out.

19:02.773 --> 19:04.983
Well, whaddya know…

19:05.025 --> 19:07.861
I can't hide anything from you,
Rohan-sensei.

19:07.986 --> 19:10.655
All right, I confess.
Here's the deal.

19:12.449 --> 19:15.827
I'm begging you!
Please play Cee-Io with me!

19:15.952 --> 19:17.662
Cee-Io?

19:17.871 --> 19:20.248
Okay, let me be perfectly honest…

19:20.540 --> 19:23.376
It's summer,
and I'm totally strapped for cash.

19:23.543 --> 19:28.043
Well, I do have 30,000 yen.
That's all I got to my name.

19:28.423 --> 19:29.757
But…

19:29.883 --> 19:33.177
Nowadays, 30,000 yen won't get you
more than a couple of visits to

19:33.220 --> 19:35.597
the amusement park and some food.

19:36.098 --> 19:38.600
So I either make me some dough,
or go flat broke.

19:39.142 --> 19:40.726
Take a risk and enjoy the thrill!

19:40.769 --> 19:43.104
Isn't that what being young
is all about?

19:43.146 --> 19:45.773
I think so at least! Don't you?!

19:48.652 --> 19:52.280
Look, let me be frank.
I've never liked you.

19:52.489 --> 19:56.618
So why in god's name
should I play Cee-Io with you?

19:56.952 --> 19:58.411
I guess you're right.

19:58.453 --> 20:02.290
You're not exactly
hurting for cash,

20:02.749 --> 20:05.960
- there's no reason for you to play.
- But… All right.

20:06.128 --> 20:08.213
Huh?! You'll do it?

20:08.255 --> 20:11.216
I don't dislike games,
besides, I'm fascinated.

20:11.341 --> 20:12.967
Come around to the back.

20:13.301 --> 20:15.636
Thank you, Rohan-sensei.

20:19.433 --> 20:22.727
THE SHOOTER ROLLS 3 DICE
INTO THE BOWL
THIS WILL RESULT IN WINNING DOUBLE
THE LARGER NUMBER WINS
(HERE, THE 6)
THIS WILL RESULT IN PAYING DOUBLE

20:19.683 --> 20:21.351
Do these rules work for you?

20:21.601 --> 20:22.685
Looks good to me.

20:23.061 --> 20:24.562
Each chip is worth 1,000 yen.

20:24.771 --> 20:26.481
Try to roll the three dice
into the bowl,

20:26.565 --> 20:28.650
if even one falls out, you lose.

20:29.109 --> 20:30.068
Got it.

20:30.277 --> 20:33.613
All right. The rules can go here.

20:33.822 --> 20:36.324
- Okay, let's get this game started!
- Wait.

20:36.575 --> 20:38.660
We won't be using that dice.

20:38.702 --> 20:39.452
Huh?!

20:39.744 --> 20:42.705
We'll be using these dice
I had in the house.

20:44.291 --> 20:48.791
U-Um, is there something
you don't like about my dice?

20:49.212 --> 20:52.673
Not really. I feel inclined
to use mine instead, that's all.

20:52.799 --> 20:53.841
And…

20:53.925 --> 20:58.054
When I mentioned I was fascinated,
it wasn't by Cee-Io.

20:58.263 --> 21:01.182
I was fascinated by
the prospect of swiping 30,000 yen

21:01.224 --> 21:03.059
from your almost yenless hands.

21:04.144 --> 21:07.021
When you lose,
I expect you to pay in full.

21:07.147 --> 21:10.066
I don't care how much we've
been through together, Josuke.

21:15.655 --> 21:19.700
<i>Yes! Those dice are actually the alien!</i>

21:19.743 --> 21:23.413
<i>I snuck them into his house
when he wasn't looking!</i>

21:23.497 --> 21:25.624
<i>Oh, I am so bad</i>

21:25.916 --> 21:27.208
<i>It won't be a ton,</i>

21:27.292 --> 21:30.586
<i>but you're about to fund
my summer vacay, Rohan-sensei</i>

21:30.754 --> 21:33.381
Now, shall we determine
who gets to go first.

21:34.674 --> 21:35.841
A four.

21:37.719 --> 21:38.594
Yes!

21:38.845 --> 21:41.305
Well, looks like you're first.
Roll.

21:41.515 --> 21:42.265
Ow!

21:42.349 --> 21:42.849
O…

21:42.849 --> 21:46.644
O-Ow! I just banged my hand
into the table.

21:50.315 --> 21:52.191
Just place your bet
and role the dice.

21:52.359 --> 21:53.610
R-Right…

21:53.902 --> 21:58.402
I-I think I'll start off with two,
so then, 2,000 yen.

21:58.865 --> 22:00.283
Got it, here's two chips.

22:00.575 --> 22:01.617
If I roll a one, a two,
and a three,

22:01.701 --> 22:03.703
I'll have to pay double,

22:03.870 --> 22:07.081
so I just have to avoid
one, two, and three at all costs.

22:07.374 --> 22:09.084
Just stay away from
one, two, and three!

22:09.167 --> 22:11.377
I can't get one, two, and three!

22:13.463 --> 22:15.590
The first roll calls for
a light touch I think.

22:15.840 --> 22:17.591
Always gotta warm up…

22:17.676 --> 22:19.803
Here we go… Nice and gentle.

22:21.304 --> 22:22.638
How's that?!

22:24.140 --> 22:25.266
- Huh?!
- What?

22:25.517 --> 22:27.477
It's an omen…

22:27.644 --> 22:28.728
What?

22:28.770 --> 22:31.314
<i>Triple sixes, AKA "omen."</i>

22:31.398 --> 22:34.484
<i>Josuke wins five times
what he wagered from Rohan.</i>

22:34.734 --> 22:37.945
You dumb ass! You can't just
start with that kind of hand!

22:38.113 --> 22:39.364
E-Er, I mean…

22:39.406 --> 22:41.658
I mean talk about dumb luck!

22:41.783 --> 22:44.535
A triple six and five times
the winnings…

22:44.578 --> 22:47.122
It almost looks like I'm cheating!

22:51.251 --> 22:54.671
Hmph. So you've already
earned 10,000 yen in change.

22:54.879 --> 22:57.298
- I'm in disbelief myself…
- Let's continue.

22:57.382 --> 22:59.258
I guess I'm next then.

22:59.384 --> 23:02.303
I want to recover
what I just lost, so I'm…

23:03.263 --> 23:04.931
going with ten.

23:05.015 --> 23:06.474
Ten?

23:06.558 --> 23:07.600
All right! There!

23:12.022 --> 23:14.315
<i>One, two, and three.
The wager is doubled!</i>

23:13.690 --> 23:17.193
THIS WILL RESULT IN PAYING DOUBLE
THE SHOOTER ROLLS 3 DICE
INTO THE BOWL

23:14.357 --> 23:17.214
<i>Rohan must pay double his wager.</i>

23:17.444 --> 23:21.156
<i>He's taking it too far!
It's getting obvious!</i>

23:21.239 --> 23:24.617
<i>Does this alien have
any concept of holding back?</i>

23:28.204 --> 23:32.374
<i>Shit… He's gotta think
things are fishy now!</i>

23:38.298 --> 23:41.509
EPISODE 28
HIGHWAY GO GO, PART 1
